#
# ⚠ THIS IS A REVIEW REQUIREMENT, NOT AN ACCESS CONTROL.
# It cannot stop anyone from CHANGING a path. It only requests — or, with
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled on the protected branch, requires —
# an approval from the named owner on the PR that changes it. Anyone holding
# write access to this repository can write to every path in it. GitHub has no
# path-scoped write permission: not for a user, not for a team, not on any
# plan. "Write access scoped to /tenants/osa/" is therefore a review convention
# plus branch protection, and nothing else. Say it that way to partners rather
# than implying the folder is a wall.
#
# ⚠ AN OWNER MUST BE A HANDLE THAT RESOLVES, AND MUST HOLD WRITE ACCESS.
# GitHub silently ignores a CODEOWNERS line naming an owner it cannot resolve,
# or one who lacks write access — the path is then simply unowned, and nothing
# in the UI says so. This file previously read @clearskyenergy/core and
# @clearskyenergy/jv-osa. `clearskyenergy` is a PERSONAL account and personal
# accounts have no teams, so BOTH matched nobody and every path below was
# unowned. If this repository moves to a GitHub organisation, restore the team
# form; until then an owner is an individual handle.
# ============================================================================

# Default: ClearSky reviews everything.
*                                     @clearskyenergy

